IMPORT prelude

-- Judicial Proceedings (Regulation of Reports) Act 1960 (Singapore) -- what may not be printed or published about court
-- proceedings (s 2), who can be convicted and of what (s 3), the Public Prosecutor's consent (s 4), and the savings (s 5).
-- The whole operative Act (ss 2 to 5); s 1 is the short title.
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/JPRRA1960.txt. The deposit says it "incorporates
-- all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021 and comes into operation on 31 December 2021". Its Legislative History lists
-- one amending Act, the Criminal Procedure Code 2010 (Act 15 of 2010, s 430 read with item 56 of the Sixth Schedule, in force
-- 2 January 2011); the sections carry no amendment annotations, so what that amendment changed is not shown.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0051 in ../../../requirements.jsonl: Tier 2 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. The requirement asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked
-- a sharper question yet. The Act is five sections long, so nothing operative is left out. Not encoded: what "indecent" or
-- "calculated to injure public morals" means (an input flag, decided by a court), what counts as "publish" for online posting,
-- and the interaction with other reporting restrictions elsewhere in the statute book (none was read).
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules conventions. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Judicial Proceedings (Regulation of Reports) Act 1960`

DECLARE Proceedings IS ONE OF
    `divorce`
    `dissolution of marriage`
    `nullity of marriage`
    `judicial separation`
    `restitution of conjugal rights`
    `a criminal trial`
    `a civil claim`
    `a maintenance or custody application`

-- s 2(1)(b) names exactly five kinds: "divorce, dissolution of marriage, nullity of marriage, judicial separation or restitution
-- of conjugal rights". A criminal trial, a civil claim, and (an inference from the list) a free-standing maintenance or custody
-- application are not among them, so only s 2(1)(a) reaches them.
GIVEN `the kind` IS A Proceedings
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the proceedings are matrimonial under section 2(1)(b)` IF
    CONSIDER `the kind`
    WHEN `divorce` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `dissolution of marriage` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `nullity of marriage` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `judicial separation` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `restitution of conjugal rights` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `2(1)(b) -- the four permitted particulars`

-- s 2(1)(b): in matrimonial proceedings it is unlawful to publish "any particulars other than the following":
--   (i) "the names, addresses and occupations of the parties and witnesses";
--   (ii) "a concise statement of the charges, the defences and countercharges in support of which evidence has been given";
--   (iii) "submissions on any point of law arising in the course of the proceedings and the decision of the court on the
--        submissions";
--   (iv) "the decision of the court and any observations made by the court in giving that decision".
-- Everything else is out: the evidence itself, a charge on which no evidence was given, and (by inference from (i), which names
-- only "parties and witnesses") the name of a child who did not testify, the parties' ages, or a photograph.
DECLARE Particular IS ONE OF
    `the names of the parties`
    `the address of a witness`
    `the occupation of a party`
    `a concise statement of a charge supported by evidence`
    `a concise statement of a defence supported by evidence`
    `a charge on which no evidence was given`
    `a submission on a point of law and the decision on it`
    `the decision and the court's observations`
    `a witness's testimony in detail`
    `the name of a child who did not testify`
    `the ages of the parties`
    `a photograph of a party`

GIVEN `the particular` IS A Particular
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the particular is in the permitted list` IF
    CONSIDER `the particular`
    WHEN `the names of the parties` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the address of a witness` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the occupation of a party` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a concise statement of a charge supported by evidence` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a concise statement of a defence supported by evidence` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a submission on a point of law and the decision on it` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the decision and the court's observations` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 2(2): "Nothing in subsection (1)(b) shall be held to permit the publication of anything contrary to subsection (1)(a)." So even
-- a permitted particular may not be published if it is indecent matter calculated to injure public morals -- the court's
-- observations included.
GIVEN `the kind` IS A Proceedings, `the particular` IS A Particular, `indecent and injurious to morals` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the particular may be reported` IF
        (NOT `indecent and injurious to morals`)
    AND (    (NOT `the proceedings are matrimonial under section 2(1)(b)` `the kind`)
         OR  `the particular is in the permitted list` `the particular`)

§§ `2 and 5 -- whether a publication is unlawful`

-- s 2(1): "It shall not be lawful to print or publish, or cause or procure to be printed or published -- (a) in relation to any
-- judicial proceedings any indecent matter or indecent medical, surgical or physiological details being matter or details the
-- publication of which would be calculated to injure public morals; or (b) [matrimonial proceedings] any particulars other than
-- [the four]."
-- s 5: "Nothing in this Act shall apply to -- (a) the printing of any pleading, transcript of evidence or other document for use in
-- connection with any judicial proceedings or the communication thereof to persons concerned in the proceedings; (b) the printing
-- or publishing of any notice or report in pursuance of the directions of the court; or (c) ... any separate volume or part of any
-- bona fide series of law reports which do not form part of any other publication and consists solely of reports of proceedings in
-- courts of law, or in any publication of a technical character bona fide intended for circulation among members of the legal or
-- medical profession."
DECLARE Publication HAS
    `about judicial proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
    `kind of proceedings` IS A Proceedings
    `contains indecent matter injurious to public morals` IS A BOOLEAN
    `contains a particular outside the permitted list` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a court document printed for the proceedings or sent to those concerned` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is published under the directions of the court` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a bona fide law report series or professional technical publication` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the publication` IS A Publication
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 5 saves the publication` IF
        `the publication`'s `is a court document printed for the proceedings or sent to those concerned`
    OR  `the publication`'s `is published under the directions of the court`
    OR  `the publication`'s `is a bona fide law report series or professional technical publication`

GIVEN `the publication` IS A Publication
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the publication contravenes section 2` IF
        `the publication`'s `about judicial proceedings`
    AND (NOT `section 5 saves the publication` `the publication`)
    AND (    `the publication`'s `contains indecent matter injurious to public morals`
         OR  (    `the proceedings are matrimonial under section 2(1)(b)` (`the publication`'s `kind of proceedings`)
              AND `the publication`'s `contains a particular outside the permitted list`))

§§ `3 and 4 -- who can be convicted, and the penalty`

-- s 3: "Any person who acts in contravention of section 2 shall be guilty of an offence ... Provided that no person, other than the
-- proprietor, editor, printer or publisher, shall be liable to be convicted under this Act."
-- s 4: "No prosecution for an offence under this Act shall be commenced without the consent of the Public Prosecutor."
-- s 2 reaches anyone who "cause[s] or procure[s]" publication, so a reporter or a party who feeds the story contravenes s 2 -- but
-- the proviso means only the four roles can be convicted.
DECLARE Role IS ONE OF
    `the proprietor`
    `the editor`
    `the printer`
    `the publisher`
    `the reporter who wrote it`
    `a party who supplied the details`

GIVEN `the role` IS A Role
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the role can be convicted` IF
    CONSIDER `the role`
    WHEN `the proprietor` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the editor` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the printer` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the publisher` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the publication` IS A Publication, `the role` IS A Role
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person may be convicted` IF
        `the publication contravenes section 2` `the publication`
    AND `the role can be convicted` `the role`

GIVEN `the publication` IS A Publication, `the role` IS A Role, `the Public Prosecutor consented` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a prosecution may be commenced` IF
        `the person may be convicted` `the publication` `the role`
    AND `the Public Prosecutor consented`

-- s 3: "a fine not exceeding $1,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding one year or to both".
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine in dollars` MEANS 1000

GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in months` MEANS 12

GIVEN `fine` IS A NUMBER, `months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the sentence is within section 3` IF
        `fine` AT MOST `the maximum fine in dollars`
    AND `months` AT MOST `the maximum imprisonment in months`
    AND `fine` AT LEAST 0
    AND `months` AT LEAST 0
